@page "/reviewer-checklist"

<PageTitle>Reviewer Checklist - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<PageHero Eyebrow="OPERATIONSFLOW / PORTFOLIO REVIEW"
          Title="Reviewer Checklist"
          Subtitle="Use this checklist to review the Week 3 local/free OperationsFlow build: SQL-backed login, roles, permissions, evidence workflow, document library, data quality, reports, traceability, and Week 4 Microsoft 365 production direction."
          BadgeText="Review Ready"
          BadgeClass="of-badge of-badge-success">
    <Actions>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/demo-guide">Demo Guide</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/business-value">Business Value</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-primary" href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a>
    </Actions>
</PageHero>

<PurposeNote Title="Purpose" Icon="✅">
    <p>
        This page gives a reviewer a structured way to verify that OperationsFlow is more than a static dashboard.
        It now includes a local/free authentication system, SQL-backed roles, evidence capture, review controls, reports, and a realistic Week 4 Microsoft 365 production path.
    </p>
</PurposeNote>

<MetricGrid>
    <MetricCard Title="Local Auth"
                Value="Ready"
                Detail="Login, logout, persistent session, and SQL-backed users."
                Icon="🔐"
                Tone="success" />

    <MetricCard Title="Evidence"
                Value="Ready"
                Detail="Record attachments, document library, and activity traceability."
                Icon="📎"
                Tone="info" />

    <MetricCard Title="Review"
                Value="Ready"
                Detail="Data quality and reports show missing evidence and coverage."
                Icon="📊"
                Tone="warning" />

    <MetricCard Title="Week 4"
                Value="Defined"
                Detail="OAuth2, SharePoint/Graph, and production deployment path."
                Icon="☁️"
                Tone="default" />
</MetricGrid>

<TableCard Title="Authentication review checklist"
           Subtitle="Week 3 now includes a working local/free login system.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Check</th>
                <th>Expected Result</th>
                <th>Why It Matters</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Login landing page</span></td>
                <td>The app opens to the login page at <strong>/</strong>.</td>
                <td>Shows the system has an access boundary instead of exposing all pages by default.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Demo accounts</span></td>
                <td>Admin, Manager, Reviewer, Worker, and Viewer accounts can be demonstrated.</td>
                <td>Shows different business access profiles.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Password handling</span></td>
                <td>Passwords are hashed, not stored as plain text.</td>
                <td>Shows the local/free version avoids unsafe password storage.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Persistent login</span></td>
                <td>Refreshing the browser keeps the user signed in.</td>
                <td>Shows the app can restore a local session and reload the account from SQL.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Logout</span></td>
                <td>The sidebar shows the signed-in user and a visible logout button.</td>
                <td>Shows the user has a clear way to end the local session.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Protected navigation</span></td>
                <td>Protected pages require login before access.</td>
                <td>Shows navigation is not purely cosmetic; the app checks login state.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Role model</span></td>
                <td>User Roles page shows users, roles, permission matrix, and external login link prep.</td>
                <td>Shows the app understands local users/roles and future OAuth2 account linking.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<TableCard Title="Workflow and evidence checklist"
           Subtitle="These checks prove the operational workflow loop.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Check</th>
                <th>Expected Result</th>
                <th>Why It Matters</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Dashboard</span></td>
                <td>Dashboard shows live local demo metrics across work orders, corrective actions, documents, risk, training, and document intake.</td>
                <td>Gives reviewers a fast operational overview.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Work Order attachments</span></td>
                <td>Work Order details include the reusable RecordAttachments panel.</td>
                <td>Shows evidence can be attached to work records.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Corrective Action attachments</span></td>
                <td>Corrective Action details include the reusable RecordAttachments panel.</td>
                <td>Shows follow-up actions can carry proof and supporting files.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Document Intake attachments</span></td>
                <td>Document Intake details include the reusable RecordAttachments panel.</td>
                <td>Shows admin/document workflows can capture source files and review evidence.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Document Library</span></td>
                <td>Files from multiple modules appear in a central library.</td>
                <td>Gives reviewers one evidence surface instead of forcing record-by-record hunting.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Activity Log</span></td>
                <td>Upload/delete and workflow events appear in Activity Log.</td>
                <td>Shows traceability and reviewer/audit visibility.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<TableCard Title="Quality and reporting checklist"
           Subtitle="These checks show the app can review operational completeness, not just store records.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Check</th>
                <th>Expected Result</th>
                <th>Why It Matters</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Missing evidence checks</span></td>
                <td>Data Quality flags overdue/high/needs-review records that have no attached evidence.</td>
                <td>Shows the app can identify weak records and follow-up gaps.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Evidence coverage report</span></td>
                <td>Reports page shows attached file totals and missing evidence counts.</td>
                <td>Gives managers a reviewable measure of evidence completeness.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Record links</span></td>
                <td>Missing evidence rows link back to record detail pages.</td>
                <td>Shows reports are actionable, not just summary numbers.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Management action report</span></td>
                <td>Reports recommend attaching evidence where important records are incomplete.</td>
                <td>Shows the app pushes practical follow-up behaviour.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">CSV exports</span></td>
                <td>Export endpoints are available for review/reporting workflows.</td>
                <td>Shows a path toward Power BI or external reporting.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<div class="of-two-column-grid">
    <InfoPanel Title="Week 3 review notes"
               Subtitle="What the reviewer should understand about the local/free version."
               Tone="success">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Local/free version:</strong>
                <span>Runs without Microsoft 365 licensing.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>SQL-backed auth:</strong>
                <span>Users, roles, permissions, and external login links are represented in the app database.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Evidence workflow:</strong>
                <span>Files can be attached to records and reviewed centrally.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Traceability:</strong>
                <span>Activity Log records workflow and evidence events.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Reporting:</strong>
                <span>Data Quality and Reports expose missing evidence and coverage.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>

    <InfoPanel Title="Week 4 review notes"
               Subtitle="What is intentionally left for the licensed/live version."
               Tone="warning">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Microsoft OAuth2:</strong>
                <span>Production login through Microsoft account identity.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Account linking:</strong>
                <span>Microsoft identity maps to LocalUser through ExternalLoginLinks.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>SharePoint storage:</strong>
                <span>Graph-backed file provider replaces local storage.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Production deployment:</strong>
                <span>Hosted environment, secrets, backup, retention, and tenant setup.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Hardening:</strong>
                <span>Production policies, audit expectations, and operational support boundaries.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>
</div>

<GuidanceNote Title="Reviewer conclusion" Icon="🏁" Tone="info">
    <p>
        A strong review outcome is not “this is already enterprise production.” A strong review outcome is:
        OperationsFlow proves the local business workflow, SQL-backed authentication, evidence traceability, and a realistic path to Microsoft 365 production implementation.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>